    "kicker": "Connect day 8 and day 10: how you spend the training budget counts.",
    "fullText": "On day 8 you saw training costs climb from about $900 for the 2017 Transformer to an estimated $78 million for GPT-4. On day 10 you met DeepMind's Chinchilla: 70 billion parameters trained on 1.4 trillion tokens, about 20 tokens per parameter.\n\nChinchilla used the same compute as the 280-billion-parameter Gopher and outperformed it, along with GPT-3, which had 175 billion parameters trained on 300 billion tokens.\n\nWhen compute costs tens of millions, the split between model size and data decides what you get for the money.",
